---Similarly to Layer, paged layers supports arbitrary positioning and layout of child components on them, however they
---also provide functionality to switch between different pages (or tabs as they're often called), allowing different
---sets of components to reside in each page.
---
---The individual pages can have icons and labels defined for them, which are used by PagedLayerHeader components to
---provide a basic page selection UI.
---@class ui.PagedLayer : ui.ComponentCollection
---@field activePage integer The currently active page, displayed to the user.
---@field numPages integer
---@field numBuiltinPages integer (Read-only) The number of statically built-in pages on this paged layer. Always zero for dynamically created paged layers.
---@field contentMargin ui.Margin (Modifiable Contents) Offsets used to determine the inner content area for this component.
---@field backgroundSprite ui.SpriteData (Modifiable Contents) Sprite properties used for the background.
ui.PagedLayer = {}

---Creates a new PagedLayer on the specified parent.
---
---Warning: Creating a component can fail if there's already a component on that parent with the same category ID and
---dynamic ID, or if those are omitted and the application is unable to generate a valid ID for the component.
---@param parent ui.ComponentCollection Parent component to create this paged layer in.
---@param categoryID? integer Category ID used to identify this component. Defaults to the parent's category ID if not specified.
---@param dynamicID? integer Dynamic ID used to identify this component. Defaults to auto-incrementing from the parent's dynamic ID if not specified.
---@return ui.PagedLayer # The newly created paged layer. The caller must set its layout and visual information afterwards.
function ui.PagedLayer.new(parent, categoryID, dynamicID) end

---Sets whether the user can switch to the specified page through a paged layer header.
---
---Disabling a page doesn't prevent it from being switched to via scripts using the `activePage` property.
---@param pageIndex integer Index for the page to access.
---@param enabled boolean Controls whether or not the user can switch to that page manually.
function ui.PagedLayer:SetPageEnabled(pageIndex, enabled) end

---Gets whether the user can switch to the specified page through a paged layer header.
---@param pageIndex integer Index for the page to access.
---@return boolean # True if the page exists and is enabled, false otherwise.
function ui.PagedLayer:GetPageEnabled(pageIndex) end

---Sets the text label displayed for the specified page in a paged layer header.
---@param pageIndex integer Index for the page to access.
---@param label string Text to display for this page in a paged layer header.
function ui.PagedLayer:SetPageLabel(pageIndex, label) end

---Gets the text label displayed for the specified page in a paged layer header.
---@param pageIndex integer Index for the page to access.
---@return string # Text to display for this page in a paged layer header, or an empty string if not specified or if the page is missing.
function ui.PagedLayer:GetPageLabel(pageIndex) end

---Sets the ID for the sprite to display as an icon for the specified page in a paged layer header.
---@param pageIndex integer Index for the page to access.
---@param iconSpriteID integer ID for the sprite to use as an icon for this page.
function ui.PagedLayer:SetPageIcon(pageIndex, iconSpriteID) end

---Gets the ID for the sprite to display as an icon for the specified page in a paged layer header.
---@param pageIndex integer Index for the page to access.
---@return integer # ID for the sprite to use as an icon for this page, or -1 if not specified or if the page is missing.
function ui.PagedLayer:GetPageIcon(pageIndex) end

---Creates a new PagedLayerHeader on the specified parent, and associates it with this paged layer, allowing it to
---retrieve labels and icons for the available pages.
---
---Warning: Creating a component can fail if there's already a component on that parent with the same category ID and
---dynamic ID, or if those are omitted and the application is unable to generate a valid ID for the component.
---@param parent ui.ComponentCollection Parent component to create this paged layer header in.
---@param categoryID? integer Category ID used to identify this component. Defaults to the parent's category ID if not specified.
---@param dynamicID? integer Dynamic ID used to identify this component. Defaults to auto-incrementing from the parent's dynamic ID if not specified.
---@return ui.PagedLayerHeader # The newly created paged layer header associated with this paged layer. The caller must set its layout and visual information afterwards.
function ui.PagedLayer:AddHeader(parent, categoryID, dynamicID) end

---These components are directly associated with an individual PagedLayer, and provide a basic UI to allow the user to
---switch between the various pages.
---
---Page information is retrieved from the associated PagedLayer, with labels and icons being displayed in page index
---order on this header. Optionally, in addition to that, an icon can also be displayed for disabled pages to indicate
---their status.
---
---Warning: Although a paged layer can be associated with any number of headers, you should avoid doing so as there's no
---benefit to it at the moment and support for that may be removed in the future.
---@class ui.PagedLayerHeader : ui.Component
---@field target ui.PagedLayer The paged layer associated with this header, and where page information is being sourced retrieved from.
---@field isHorizontal boolean Controls whether this header uses a horizontal or vertical layout.
---@field contentMargin ui.Margin (Modifiable Contents) Offsets used to determine the inner content area for this component.
---@field pageHeaderMargin ui.Margin (Modifiable Contents) Offsets used to determine the inner content area for each page element.
---@field entryText ui.TextData (Modifiable Contents) Text properties used when displaying entries for this combo.
---@field backgroundSprite ui.SpriteData (Modifiable Contents) Sprite properties used for the background.
---@field disabledPageIcon ui.SpriteData (Modifiable Contents) Sprite properties used for the icon displayed on disabled pages.
---@field pageHeaderSprite ui.SpriteData (Modifiable Contents) Sprite properties used for the the individual page elements.
local PagedLayerHeader = {}
